<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74761" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργ-άς</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any well-watered,
				fertile spot of land, meadow-land,</i> partially wooded, with
			or without cultivated fields, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.325.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				340
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				445
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1162
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.41
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ὀργάδα τὰν Ἀχέροντος</span>
			<u>Hymn.Is.</u> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Not.Arch.</u>
				4.212
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>rich tract of land sacred to the gods</i>: such a tract between
			Athens and Megara, sacred to Demeter and Persephone, was specially
			called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὀ.</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὰ ὀ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				13.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				35
			</span></i> P., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				3.4.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.204.8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i> ; similarly perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργή</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				4.46
			</span></i> (s.v.l.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
